WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:07.970
Hey, David, when will you start going to restaurants,
the gym, the movies, traveling and doing all

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.160
of your normal life after a Corona virus?

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.160
I don't know.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.809
I've been thinking about this a lot.

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:15.900
Talking to friends and family.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.340
And I'm planning to get an antibody test next
week or the week after.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:26.170
And it's conceivable that my behavior may
be different if it turns out that I already

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.170
had the virus.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.160
I think that that might affect my behavior
to some degree.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.930
But I'm not just thinking about myself.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:37.399
I'm thinking about do I want to be seeing
my parents when they start dying down?

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:43.789
Because if so, I probably need to do the responsible
thing and not go to some of these places,

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:48.550
particularly if I don't have the antibodies,
if I want to be around my parents.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:53.350
So I think for me, the gym seems pretty far
off.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.450
That seems like a cesspool of germs and contagion.

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.940
I never go to the movies as it is.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:03.139
The last movie I saw was not the latest Star
Wars, but the previous one is the last time

00:01:03.139 --> 00:01:04.139
I went to the movies.

00:01:04.139 --> 00:01:07.049
I think that was three or four years ago here
in Boston.

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:08.660
So I think I'm fine without going to the movies.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:09.920
I don't really care about the movies.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:18.180
For me, the big things really are seeing friends,
particularly at beer gardens or going to restaurants,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.430
going to cafes, etc..

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:28.530
I'm feeling like if they are going to start
opening some of those up with reduced capacity,

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:35.479
my favorite cafe said we're going to operate
at 20 percent capacity and the employees will

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:36.590
wear masks.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.310
And you know, it's kind of hard to have a
mask on when when you're eating or drinking,

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.960
but I would probably go and sit with my laptop.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.840
If the numbers keep declining in Massachusetts
the way they have been, if in three weeks

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.009
those places start to open, I'd probably go
and sit with my laptop for two hours, have

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:54.100
a coffee, then come home, wash my hands.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.920
And I think I would be comfortable with that.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.539
Travel is a real question mark.

00:01:58.539 --> 00:01:59.799
I don't know.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:04.969
I had a bunch of trips canceled, including
I was supposed to be in L.A. on the Joe Rogan

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:10.450
program last week and try I had vacations
planned.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.950
I don't know when that's going to resume,
but I will probably just look at, you know,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.380
when when we travels down air travels down
95 percent.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:22.620
My senses where I'm not gonna be the first
person to get back on a plane when I see the

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.100
numbers recovering.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:31.700
Particularly evaluating the case cases in
Massachusetts and where I would be flying

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.720
to all kind of make that call when it comes
to it.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.810
I would love to be able to go somewhere in
August at this point.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.040
I don't know if we'll still be in wave one
or maybe already in wave two.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.770
Or maybe things would be OK to travel.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.770
I don't know.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:47.420
But I'm not making any any sort of bigger
decisions about that right now.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.769
Curious to hear where your mind is.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:49.870
I know I have.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.770
I have friends who have been traveling throughout
and I have friends who are saying they're

00:02:54.770 --> 00:03:01.650
not traveling until 2022 or going to restaurants,
period, for any time in the foreseeable future.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.739
I guess I'm kind of in the middle and I'm
going to make decisions on on a case by case

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:05.739
basis.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.159
Right now, I'm looking to May 18 to see how
much two cases hopefully keep declining in

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:11.239
Massachusetts.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:15.890
And will our governor, Charlie Baker, open
anything up on that date?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.890
Let me know your thoughts.

